  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 143 PM CDT Mon Aug 24 2026\n\nShowers and thunderstorms are possible tonight into early Tuesday \nmorning as a wave skirts by to the north and west. For early this\nevening, instability grows across central SD, with CAPE values of\n2000-3000 J/kg, but only marginal shear. Initially storms will be\nmost likely west of the area, but some development could creep into\nGregory and Brule counties. Capping may preclude any development,\nso only low confidence in storms actually developing. Later \ntonight into early Tuesday morning a tail of convection could \nbuild south towards highway 14 and into pars of southwest MN. \nHere CAPE values of about 1000-1500 J/kg will be possible with \nminor-moderate shear. Some question as the whether we see an \nincrease in moisture around 800 mb which appears to be needed to\nproduce a few updrafts. Once again this is somewhat lower \nconfidence set up. Isolated severe weather will be possible in \nbth areas, half dollars and 70 mph winds in central SD and \nquarters and 60 mph winds in southwest MN.\n\nWarmer air aloft builds into the area Tuesday, but other than northwest \nIA the threat for showers and thunderstorms will be fairly low.\nIf there is some elevated moisture there could be a little \nactivity in the morning. Northwest IA may see just enough \ninstability and shear on Tuesday afternoon for a couple of \nstrong to severe updrafts.\n\nBehind this cooler and drier air builds into the area which appears to \nbring dry and seasonally mild conditions for Wednesday and Thursday.\n\nStronger westerly winds aloft will spread across the area Friday into\nthe weekend. This should bring occasional chances for showers \nand thunderstorms during this time. Friday night appears to be a\nbetter chance right now. As the warmer conditions and somewhat \ndeeper instability build in Friday night into Saturday isolated \nsevere storms will be possible.",
